@@ -35,6 +35,25 @@ portfire pack  show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --audience 200
 
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
+## firing what is on the shelf
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired out of whatever the
+magazine book holds, and those two are never the same. Hand any show command
+`--magazine` and every cue is drawn from real stock in firing order, carries the
+lot it came out of onto the cue sheet, and empties the oldest lot first.
+
+```
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv --pull vn2405
+```
+
+Where the shelf runs out, the nearest shell of the same calibre stands in, the
+timing and the separation are worked out from the shell that will really be in
+the tube, and the swap is reported. Where nothing will do, the cue keeps what
+was written and the show is not ready. `--pull` sets lots aside before the draw,
+which is what a recall, or a case that came off the van wet, means.
+
 ## the commands
 
 | command                        | what it answers                                |
